WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.170
Digital footprints are discovered through lawful review of public sources.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.339
Search engines can locate indexed pages, documents, profiles, and references.

00:00:10.339 --> 00:00:17.307
Public records and official websites can establish dates, ownership claims, policies, or organizational relationships.

00:00:17.307 --> 00:00:24.725
Social platforms may show public statements and professional context, but identity and authenticity require validation.

00:00:24.725 --> 00:00:28.995
Archives can preserve prior versions of public pages.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:36.413
Domain, DNS, and certificate sources can help defenders reconcile their public infrastructure with internal inventories.

00:00:36.413 --> 00:00:44.729
Public code search can reveal organizational projects, references, or accidental exposure in repositories that are legitimately accessible.

00:00:44.729 --> 00:00:49.899
Image and metadata review can provide context about published material.

00:00:49.899 --> 00:00:58.215
These activities should serve an authorized defensive or analytical purpose, not identification or tracking of private individuals.

00:00:58.215 --> 00:01:05.183
Public breach notifications can help users and organizations understand that a provider reported exposure.

00:01:05.183 --> 00:01:15.298
Notifications are context for defensive account protection; they do not authorize obtaining, trading, or using stolen data, passwords, or private records.

00:01:15.298 --> 00:01:18.669
Discovery should be documented and bounded.

00:01:18.669 --> 00:01:22.490
Record the purpose, source, date, and relevance.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:29.009
Avoid collecting unrelated personal details, entering private spaces, impersonating users, or circumventing restrictions.

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:35.077
If access requires a control you are not authorized to use, stop.

00:01:35.077 --> 00:01:39.798
Multiple discovery methods may surface the same underlying source.

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:45.866
Trace claims to origin and do not mistake repeated indexing for corroboration.

00:01:45.866 --> 00:01:56.880
The useful outcome is a validated exposure finding with enough context for remediation, not a large collection of unverified personal or technical data.
